  "id": "Compound::DB06694 - Gene::152",
  "verbalization": "Xylometazoline is shown to interact with Adra2c through multiple pathways, suggesting a potential role in modulating adrenergic signaling. The evidence indicates that Xylometazoline binds to Adra1d and Adra2a, which are both involved in Alpha-adrenergic receptor activity, and this activity is ultimately linked to Adra2c. These findings suggest that Xylometazoline may influence adrenergic signaling through the activation of adrenergic receptors, potentially affecting physiological processes regulated by these receptors. The consistent involvement of Adra2c in the pathways involving Xylometazoline highlights a possible mechanism by which Xylometazoline could modulate adrenergic signaling, though the exact functional role of Adra2c in this context remains to be fully elucidated. The integration of these pathways supports a mechanistic link between Xylometazoline and Adra2c, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm the clinical relevance of this interaction.",
